WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.080
Welcome to Grade 4 English, Unit 7:
Emotions, Behaviour, and Identity.

2
00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:11.300
In this unit you will learn how to talk about
emotions (how we feel), behaviour (how we act),

3
00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:15.340
and identity (who we are and where our family comes from).

4
00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:23.520
You will read about children who feel nervous, curious,
proud, and shy — and who learn to be gentle, polite,

5
00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:24.860
and generous to others.

6
00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:32.400
You will practise saying how you feel, giving kind
advice, and describing what makes your own family special.

7
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.920
By the end, you will be ready to understand this unit's story,

8
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:42.300
“The Day of the Play,” in which a girl
called Nadia finds her courage on stage.

9
00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:48.080
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

10
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:56.140
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name many
feelings and describe them, using words like nervous, anxious,

11
00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:57.620
proud, and curious.

12
00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:04.620
you will also describe how people behave, using
words like gentle, selfish, generous, and polite.

13
00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:11.300
you will also talk about experiences in your life using
the present perfect (“i have felt nervous before.”).

14
00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:14.580
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

15
00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:22.800
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
nervous, anxious, terrified, doubtful, curious, proud.

16
00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:28.360
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

17
00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:32.240
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

18
00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:38.280
The reading sequence includes The Day Before
the Test and Where My Family Comes From.

19
00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:40.100
Read actively.

20
00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:45.360
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

21
00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:49.580
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

22
00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:54.940
The first language focus is Present
Perfect (for life experiences).

23
00:01:55.700 --> 00:02:00.560
We use the present perfect to talk about things
we have done or felt at some time in our life,

24
00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:02.700
when the exact time does not matter.

25
00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:05.400
It connects the past to now.

26
00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:13.740
Saying “I have felt nervous before” shows the feeling
happened, and it still helps us understand ourselves today.

27
00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:21.140
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

28
00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:27.200
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1: How Do You Feel?.

29
00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:32.580
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

30
00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:36.800
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

31
00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:40.540
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

32
00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:42.300
You are ready to begin.

33
00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:49.520
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

34
00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:52.760
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

35
00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:59.160
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
